    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 40,
    "summary": "Christ brings to pass the resurrection of all men—The righteous dead go to paradise and the wicked to outer darkness to await the day of their resurrection—All things will be restored to their proper and perfect frame in the Resurrection. About 74 B.C.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Now my son, here is somewhat more I would say unto thee; for I perceive that thy mind is worried concerning the resurrection of the dead.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 40:1",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 40,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, I say unto you, that there is no resurrection—or, I would say, in other words, that this mortal does not put on immortality, this corruption does not put on incorruption—until after the coming of Christ.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 131,
            "text": "Mosiah 16:10 (10–13). TG Immortality."
          },
          {
            "start": 158,
